In article <14ak50INNc3f@agate.berkeley.edu>, labc-1ad@e260-4b.berkeley.edu (Eric van Bezooijen) writes:
|> I have a question.  I am playing my best character ever, and I managed to
|> find a pile of blessed enchant Weapon scrolls.  I quickly got my Excalibur
|> up to +11, and I started to basically mow monsters down by the dozen.  
|> However, I come to this one level, and find a scroll of Enchant Weapon,
|> have my cat walk over it (to see if it is cursed or not), use it and I
|> get the following message (more or less, don't remember exact wording):
|> 
|> "Your sword glows brightly blue for a flash, and evaporates".
|> 
|> What happened ?  Did I over-enchant it ?  Can you not enchant a weapon
|> over +11 ?
|> 

Yep, you over-enchanted it.  You were actually really lucky to get it to
+11.  There is a 2/3 chance of it exploding (or is it a 2/3 chance of it
not exploding?  I forget) if it is over +5.  So, the most you can reliably
get it to is +8 -- by reading a blessed enchant weapon scroll on a +5
weapon.
